liuqin: define liuqin_marks_draw, which the touch watch references

Patch 0219 turned the touch interrupt watch's console override into a
boot-arg-gated one:

	extern int liuqin_marks_draw;
	if (liuqin_marks_draw) {
		liuqin_console_force = 1;
	}

but nothing in the series defines that variable, so the kernel links with

	Undefined symbols for architecture arm64:
	  "_liuqin_marks_draw", referenced from:
	      _liuqin_touch_int_watch in liuqin_touch.o
	clang: error: linker command failed with exit code 1

and no kernel is produced at all (CI run 41765862904 uploaded only symbol
dumps). Define it next to the other console switches so the gate defaults to
"off", matching the pre-0219 behaviour only when a boot passes
liuqin_marks=1; the console override stays available for the diagnostics that
set it.

diff --git a/osfmk/console/serial_console.c b/osfmk/console/serial_console.c
--- a/osfmk/console/serial_console.c
+++ b/osfmk/console/serial_console.c
@@ -274,6 +274,13 @@ extern void liuqin_log_append(const char *c, int size);  /* bsd/dev/liuqin_ufs.c
  * the GUI. A panic draws again.
  */
 int liuqin_console_muted;
+/*
+ * Gate for the touch interrupt watch's console override (patch 0219). Nothing
+ * defined it, so the kernel failed to link with "_liuqin_marks_draw referenced
+ * from _liuqin_touch_int_watch". Off by default: the watch then only logs, and
+ * a boot that wants the transitions on screen passes liuqin_marks=1.
+ */
+int liuqin_marks_draw;
 /* Set around the few lines that must stay visible while the console is muted
  * (boot-phase marks, per-exec timestamps): they are the only time axis a boot
  * without a serial port has. */
 int liuqin_console_force;
